## Non-negotiable conventions (summary)

- Colors route through `ColorPalette` in `Miniti/Models/ColorPalette.swift` — never hardcode hex literals in view code.
- Typography: monospaced throughout (SF Mono macOS / Menlo iOS). Dark mode only.
- `AppState` is the single source of truth. Transient high-frequency signals go in `AudioLevelsState` / `TranscriptRuntimeState`.
- `appState.modelContext` must be wired from `@Environment(\.modelContext)` in the first view (`MainWindow.swift` macOS / `MainTabView.swift` iOS). Without it, saves silently no-op.
- Hot-path rule: never `.filter` `@Published` arrays in callbacks that fire on every transcript finalize. Iterate `.reversed()` and break on window expiry.
- Changelog: public-audience prose, no code refs. Never edit old entries. See `CHANGELOG.md`.
- macOS is shipped sandboxed. Never call `codesign --force --sign` on a bundle with entitlements without passing `--entitlements` too — that's what caused the v1.24.0 history-wipe regression.

## When making changes

1. Read `docs/patterns.md` before introducing new cross-cutting behavior.
2. If a change invalidates a documented pattern or adds a new one, update the relevant doc in the same PR.
3. For any release-adjacent change (build, sign, notarize, appcast, version files), treat `RELEASE.md` and `docs/distribution.md` as the spec — don't improvise.
